  "method": "Each candidate considered independently. Turret heads use complete yaw cylinders separately for every occupied Y layer. Gun occupied voxels use continuous one-degree pitch-interval extrema, both recoil endpoints and full yaw, retaining horizontal radius separately in one-unit Y layers. Arc parts use fixed occupied-vertex bounds. Launcher bounds include the tallest loaded missile tip across the full casing footprint. Test exact static cuboids and actual production Tripod/Ray occupied-part poses at every1-unit route distance and endpoints. Conservative envelopes can reject a harmless pose; an overlap is a restriction, not proof of an actual joint collision. Separate finite flights probe actual launches. No simultaneous-neighbour compatibility is claimed; gun upgrade2 is physically surveyed. Shared preview attack profiles differ from the active play-only tier2 profile, which belongs to campaign verification.",
